WEBVTT

NOTE Sentence timings are approximate, not word-aligned.

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.309
Suppose an instruction says: Bay three, six forty-five
p.m., and bring printed ID.

2
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:11.064
We can change its presentation while keeping those facts
fixed.

3
00:00:11.687 --> 00:00:15.655
But listen to this shorter version: Check in this
evening.

4
00:00:15.655 --> 00:00:16.612
Bring your ID.

5
00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:21.607
Now the exact place, time, and printed-copy requirement
have disappeared.

6
00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.875
There's another catch.

7
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:29.477
If the supplied location is wrong, every format can
repeat the same mistake.

8
00:00:29.477 --> 00:00:33.752
Agreement across formats doesn't verify the original
fact.

9
00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:36.843
This is a fixed-template illustration.

10
00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:42.984
Preserving facts, checking their truth, and helping a
reader understand are separate questions.
